### 1.  \(\displaystyle\left\lfloor\frac1{a_{2025}}\right\rfloor\)

\[
\frac1{a_{2025}}=\frac{2^{2^{2025}}+1}{2^{2^{2024}}}
               =2^{2^{2025}-2^{2024}}+2^{-2^{2024}}
               =2^{2^{2024}}+2^{-2^{2024}} .
\]

Since \(0<2^{-2^{2024}}<1\),

\[
\Bigl\lfloor\frac1{a_{2025}}\Bigr\rfloor = 2^{2^{2024}} .
\]

---

### 2.  Modulo \(407\)

\(407=11\cdot 37\) and \(\varphi(407)= (11-1)(37-1)=360\).  
Because \(\gcd(2,407)=1\),

\[
2^{k}\pmod{407}\quad\text{depends only on }k\bmod 360 .
\]

Thus we need  

\[
e = 2^{2024}\pmod{360}.
\]

Using modular exponentiation,

\[
e = 2^{2024}\bmod 360 = 256 .
\]

Therefore  

\[
2^{2^{2024}}\pmod{407}=2^{e}\pmod{407}=2^{256}\pmod{407}=53 .
\]

