        [Turn 10 REASONING] (2331 chars)
        \[
a_{1}=\frac25 ,\qquad a_{n}^{2}=a_{n+1}-2a_{n}^{2}a_{n+1}
\]

---

### 1.  Simplify the recurrence  

\[
a_{n}^{2}=a_{n+1}\bigl(1-2a_{n}^{2}\bigr)\Longrightarrow 
a_{n+1}= \frac{a_{n}^{2}}{1-2a_{n}^{2}} .
\]

Put  

\[
x_{n}= \frac1{a_{n}}\;(>0).
\]

Then  

\[
\frac1{x_{n+1}}=\frac{1}{x_{n}^{2}}\Big/\Bigl(1-\frac{2}{x_{n}^{2}}\Bigr)
      =\frac1{x_{n}^{2}-2},
\qquad\text{hence}\qquad
x_{n+1}=x_{n}^{2}-2 .
\]

The initial value is  

\[
x_{1}= \frac1{a_{1}}=\frac52 .
\]

Thus  

\[
x_{n+1}=x_{n}^{2}-2,\qquad x_{1}= \frac52 .
\]

---

### 2.  Closed form of \(x_{n}\)

Compute a few terms:

\[
\begin{aligned}
x_{1}&=\frac52 =\frac{2^{2}+1}{2},\\[2mm]
x_{2}&=\Bigl(\frac52\Bigr)^{2}-2=\frac{25-8}{4}= \frac{2^{4}+1}{2^{2}},\\[2mm]
x_{3}&=\Bigl(\frac{17}{4}\Bigr)^{2}-2=\frac{2^{8}+1}{2^{4}},\\
&\ \vdots
\end{aligned}
\]

The pattern is  

\[
\boxed{\,x_{n}= \frac{2^{2^{\,n}}+1}{2^{2^{\,n-1}}}\,}
      =2^{2^{\,n-1}}+2^{-2^{\,n-1}} .
\]

Indeed, if the formula holds for \(n\),

\[
x_{n+1}=x_{n}^{2}-2=
\Bigl(2^{2^{n-1}}+2^{-2^{n-1}}\Bigr)^{2}-2
      =2^{2^{n}}+2^{-2^{n}} .
\]

Thus it is true for all \(n\ge1\).

Consequently  

\[
a_{n}= \frac1{x_{n}}= \frac{2^{2^{\,n-1}}}{2^{2^{\,n}}+1},
\qquad
\frac1{a_{n}}=x_{n}=2^{2^{\,n-1}}+2^{-2^{\,n-1}} .
\]

---

### 3.  The integer part of \(\displaystyle\frac1{a_{2025}}\)

For any \(n\ge1\),

\[
0<2^{-2^{\,n-1}}<1,
\]

so  

\[
\bigl\lfloor \tfrac1{a_{n}}\bigr\rfloor
   =\bigl\lfloor 2^{2^{\,n-1}}+2^{-2^{\,n-1}}\bigr\rfloor
   =2^{2^{\,n-1}} .
\]

Hence  

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle\bigl\lfloor \tfrac1{a_{2025}}\bigr\rfloor
      =2^{2^{2024}} } .
\]

---

### 4.  Reduce \(2^{2^{2024}}\) modulo \(407\)

\(407=11\cdot 37\) (both primes).  
We compute the residue modulo each prime and combine by CRT.

*Modulo \(11\)*  

\[
\phi(11)=10,\qquad 
2^{2024}\equiv 6\pmod{10}\;(2^{4k}\equiv6\pmod{10}),
\]
\[
2^{2^{2024}}\equiv 2^{6}\equiv 64\equiv 9\pmod{11}.
\]

*Modulo \(37\)*  

\[
\phi(37)=36,\qquad 
2^{2024}\equiv 4\pmod{36},
\]
\[
2^{2^{2024}}\equiv 2^{4}=16\pmod{37}.
\]

Now solve  

\[
x\equiv 9\pmod{11},\qquad x\equiv 16\pmod{37}.
\]

Using the Chinese Remainder Theorem,

\[
x\equiv 53\pmod{407}.
\]

(Indeed, \(53\equiv9\;(11)\) and \(53\equiv16\;(37)\).)

Thus  

\[
\boxed{\bigl\lfloor \tfrac1{a_{2025}}\bigr\rfloor\pmod{407}=53 } .
\]

\[
\Vboxed{53}
\]

