                # For MTZ for Hamiltonian path, we can set u_0 = 0.
                # For each arc (i,j) with i != 0 and j != 0: u_i - u_j + N * x_{i,j} <= N-1
                # Additionally, for each vertex v != 0: sum_{j} x_{v,j} = 1 (out-degree) and sum_{i} x_{i,v} = 1 (in-degree)
                # For start vertex 0: out-degree = 1, in-degree = 0.
                # For end vertex (unknown), we will have in-degree = 1, out-degree = 0.
                # To model end unspecified, we can allow start out-degree 1, start in-degree 0, and for all other vertices v != 0: out-degree - in-degree = 0 (i.e., equal). This ensures each non-start vertex has same in/out degree, which for a path means each has either (1,1) interior or (0,1) end or (1,0) start. Since start already fixed, the only other vertex can have (0,1) (end) while others have (1,1). This works.
                # So constraints: for v != 0: sum_out(v) - sum_in(v) = 0.
