        The centre of the sphere must stay at least a distance  

\[
r=\frac{\sqrt6}{36}
\]

from each face of the regular tetrahedron of side \(a=1\).

For a regular tetrahedron the inradius (distance from the centroid to any face) is  

\[
r_{\text{in}}=\frac{a\sqrt6}{12}= \frac{\sqrt6}{12}.
\]

If each face is moved inward by the same distance \(r\), the new tetrahedron is homothetic to the original with the centroid as the centre of similarity.  
Hence its inradius is  

\[
r_{\text{in}}' = r_{\text{in}}-r.
\]

Since the inradius is proportional to the side length, the scaling factor \(k\) of the side lengths is  

\[
k = \frac{r_{\text{in}}'}{r_{\text{in}}}=1-\frac{r}{r_{\text{in}}}
   =1-\frac{\frac{\sqrt6}{36}}{\frac{\sqrt6}{12}}
   =1-\frac{1}{3}= \frac{2}{3}.
\]

Thus the side length of the reachable region is  

\[
a' = k a = \frac{2}{3}.
\]

The volume of a regular tetrahedron of side \(a\) is  

\[
V_0 = \frac{a^{3}}{6\sqrt2}.
\]

Therefore the volume of the reachable region is  

\[
V = V_0\,k^{3}= \frac{1}{6\sqrt2}\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{3}
   = \frac{2\sqrt2}{81}.
\]

Now  

\[
V^{2}= \left(\frac{2\sqrt2}{81}\right)^{2}= \frac{8}{6561},
\qquad
\frac{1}{V^{2}} = \frac{6561}{8}=820.125.
\]

Hence  

\[
\boxed{\left\lfloor\frac{1}{V^{2}}\right\rfloor = 820}.
\]

